{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>After caught.</b> After it was caught in the thicket by its horns. And if the letter is a chet, then נאחז has a kamatz gadol and you must supply the word \"was.\" Likewise its sense is: after it was caught, and many like it. Others say that אחר is joined with \"Abraham lifted his eyes\" (v. 13), but if that were so it would be אחרי, אחרי כן, or אחרי זאת, as is the rule of the language in every known instance."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "I resolved חי\"ת as a reference to the letter chet (the second letter of אחר); this is the standard reading. If the word נאחז has a kamatz gadol under the alef, it indicates a passive participle construction requiring a supplied copula. The last clause, literally 'in everything known,' I render as 'in every known instance.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:25.569130996Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}